  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">DANIDA Strategic Partnership 2022-24 - SH</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project will target members of local organizations who have experience in humanitarian work in strategic or technical roles, such as programme managers and technical team leads, who wish to learn how to incorporate gender in humanitarian action and develop gender leadership within their organizations. Potential participants will be identified through an open call for application for local organization and their members. These will be invited to submit the organizational interest letters alongside their individual Curriculum Vitaes (CVs). Oxfam in collaboration with relevant stakeholders will review all incoming applications and select local organization and their members that best fit the profile. A clear set of criteria will be applied for the selection of applicants, which will be shared in advance with all participants. Moreover, the project will also target community members and/or other stakeholders through community -led initiatives that will be implemented by the selected organizations after completing the training. These initiatives will be designed based on community needs identified by the organizations themselves and according to their mandate.</narrative>
  </description>
